+ "prepare:1": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You plan one illustration of one moment of a work's text. You get the moment with its neighbours in the same story section, the work brief, the era, the section cast and a SECTION LOOK GUIDE. Return only JSON.\\n- Draw one scene at one instant: no collage and no sequence of steps. If the moment recounts several actions, pick one representative instant. If it has no event (a list, genealogy, law, saying or greeting), illustrate its content or setting through people, places and things, never as a written document.\\n- Show what the moment is about. When the moment is mostly someone's words (a prophecy, oracle, poem, proverb, prayer, letter, argument or teaching, or a story, parable, vision or memory being told), draw what the words describe and leave the speaker, writer and listeners out, unless the text shows them inside that scene (a visionary within the vision). Never put a speaker, writer or listener into a scene their words only describe, and never make them a figure of their own words.\\n- In `selectedCast`, list every section cast entry that will be visible: people, groups, places and objects. Give a few words of the text for each. Leave out cast who are elsewhere or only mentioned. Anyone without a cast entry may appear as an unnamed role or crowd when the moment needs them.\\n- Describe pose, action, placement and situational detail. Leave fixed appearance to canon, name no art style, and ask for no visible writing: books, letters and papers stay closed or folded, and the jurors' slates show no writing, and signs and boards are blank. Describe only what can be seen; leave out unseen or invisible beings, because anything named gets drawn. Keep every depiction rule.\\n- The scene description carries this moment's place, time, light and situational clothing. The SECTION LOOK GUIDE is a suggestion for them: keep what fits this moment and change what does not. OWNER LOOK CONSTRAINTS, when given instead, are binding: keep the setting and time of day consistent with them.\\n- Write one compact scene paragraph, at most 2800 characters. It is the only description of the chosen instant; do not repeat it in separate fields.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"WORK BRIEF\\nTone: Whimsical and dreamlike, with a gently unsettling bewilderment that turns to sharp absurdity at court.\\nDepiction rules:\\n- Alice's changing size reads clearly against doors, furniture, trees and other figures.\\n- Talking animals are drawn as animals, with human posture and dress where the text gives it.\\n- Playing-card courtiers, gardeners and soldiers are flat, oblong cards with heads, arms and legs.\\n- Threats and executions stay threats or slapstick; no gore or real injury.\\n- Take no likeness, costume or prop from film or animated adaptations.\\nEra: Victorian England and its dream Wonderland. People: Alice, a young Victorian English girl, among talking animals, card courtiers and odd Wonderland folk. Dress: A Victorian child's dress and pinafore for Alice; period robes, waistcoats and hats for others. Technology: Pocket watches, oil lamps, slates and pencils; no machines or modern devices.\\nSTORY SECTION: Talk with the Cheshire Cat\\n\\nMOMENT (Pig and Pepper ¶50): The Cat only grinned when it saw Alice. It looked good-natured, she thought: still it had very long claws and a great many teeth, so she felt that it ought to be treated with respect.\\nPREVIOUS: (section starts here)\\nNEXT: “Cheshire Puss,” she began, rather timidly, as she did not at all know whether it would like the name.\\n\\nCAST ON STAGE IN THIS SECTION (id: name):\\n- alice: Alice\\n- cheshire_cat: Cheshire Cat\\n- the_duchess_s_wood: the Duchess's wood\\n\\nSECTION LOOK GUIDE (a suggestion; keep what fits this moment):\\n{\\\"place\\\":\\\"A wood of old trees\\\",\\\"timeOfDay\\\":\\\"Afternoon\\\",\\\"weather\\\":\\\"Still and dry\\\",\\\"light\\\":\\\"Dappled sunlight\\\",\\\"clothing\\\":\\\"Alice in her pinafore\\\"}\"}],\"response_format\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"scene_plan\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"focusQuote\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A few words copied from MOMENT naming what this image shows.\"},\"selectedCast\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"entryId\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"alice\",\"cheshire_cat\",\"the_duchess_s_wood\"]},\"evidence\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A few words from the text that put this entry in the scene.\"}},\"required\":[\"entryId\",\"evidence\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"description\":\"Every section cast entry visible in the image, once each: people, groups, places and objects. Empty when none is. Order the selected entries by their importance in this image, with the main subject first; this order prioritizes reference sheets within each kind.\"},\"scene\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"One compact paragraph describing one visible instant: who is where, doing what, with the relevant surroundings and changing state. Leave fixed appearance to canon and artistic treatment to the chosen style. At most 2800 characters.\"}},\"required\":[\"focusQuote\",\"selectedCast\",\"scene\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"provider\":{\"require_parameters\":true,\"order\":[\"anthropic\"],\"allow_fallbacks\":false},\"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"none\"},\"max_tokens\":2400,\"usage\":{\"include\":true}}",
+ "prepare:2": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You check an illustration plan before it is drawn. You get the moment's text with its neighbours, the depiction rules, the section cast (id, name, hasForm), the plan's selected cast ids (`present`), its scene description, any OWNER LOOK CONSTRAINTS that rendering will use, and the canon of the selected entries. Report only clear problems that a careful reader would agree with, and return an empty list when the plan is a reasonable illustration of the moment. Do not report preferences, small omissions or other valid readings. Return only JSON.\\nThe text decides who is in the scene; canon decides how they look; the scene plan decides this moment's place, time, light, clothing and action. Owner look constraints, when given, are binding.\\nKinds:\\n- unselected_figure: a section cast entry (a person, group, place or object) is clearly depicted in the scene description but its id is not in present. Use its id.\\n- outside_instant: a selected or described person or presence does not belong in this moment, such as a speaker, writer, prophet or listener put into a scene their words only describe or made a figure of their own words, the narrator of a story or vision, or someone from a different event. Use its id, or empty.\\n- not_one_instant: the description gives someone incompatible poses or places, or shows successive steps as one image.\\n- look_conflict: an OWNER LOOK CONSTRAINTS value (only when supplied) contradicts the scene, the text or the depiction rules. Quote that value.\\n- canon_conflict: the scene description contradicts a selected entry's fixed canon. Quote the scene description.\\n- missing_canon: the scene depicts a named recurring character or group with no section cast entry. Leave entryId empty.\\nFor each problem, copy a short exact phrase from the scene description or a selected id into planQuote (from an owner constraint for look_conflict) and give a one-sentence reason.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"DEPICTION RULES\\n- Alice's changing size reads clearly against doors, furniture, trees and other figures.\\n- Talking animals are drawn as animals, with human posture and dress where the text gives it.\\n- Playing-card courtiers, gardeners and soldiers are flat, oblong cards with heads, arms and legs.\\n- Threats and executions stay threats or slapstick; no gore or real injury.\\n- Take no likeness, costume or prop from film or animated adaptations.\\nSTORY SECTION: Talk with the Cheshire Cat\\n\\nMOMENT (Pig and Pepper ¶50): The Cat only grinned when it saw Alice. It looked good-natured, she thought: still it had very long claws and a great many teeth, so she felt that it ought to be treated with respect.\\nPREVIOUS: (section starts here)\\nNEXT: “Cheshire Puss,” she began, rather timidly, as she did not at all know whether it would like the name.\\n\\nSECTION CAST (id: name, hasForm):\\n- alice: Alice (hasForm: true)\\n- cheshire_cat: Cheshire Cat (hasForm: true)\\n- the_duchess_s_wood: the Duchess's wood (hasForm: true)\\n\\nSELECTED CANON (complete assigned stages; fixed identity, not source evidence):\\n- alice (stage: main, kind: character, hasForm: true): Alice: a girl of about seven with long light-brown hair, in a blue dress and white pinafore.\\n- cheshire_cat (stage: main, kind: character, hasForm: true): Cheshire Cat: a large striped cat with a very wide grin, long claws and many teeth.\\n- the_duchess_s_wood (stage: main, kind: location, hasForm: true): the Duchess's wood: tall old trees with low boughs and dappled light.\\n\\nPLAN\\npresent: alice, cheshire_cat, the_duchess_s_wood\\nscene: the Cheshire Cat grinning on a bough; grins down at Alice; a wood of old trees; Alice looking up respectfully; curious; afternoon; Alice small below, the Cat above\"}],\"response_format\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"plan_review\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\"type\":\"object\"