  "prepare:exodus-32-4:0": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You write a SECTION LOOK for an illustrated edition: one short shared visual description reused by every image of a story section, so that independently generated images of the section agree with each other. Return only JSON.\\nRules: each value is one or two short phrases, at most 200 characters. Describe only what stays the same across the whole section: place, time of day, weather, light, and situational clothing or props. Leave out poses, actions and individual moments, and do not restate anyone's fixed appearance; canon does that. If the section spans a change (night into morning), say so once. Obey the work brief's depiction rules. Mention no text or written elements.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"WORK BRIEF\\nTone: Reverent, grounded and epic; grief, hope and human dignity without spectacle.\\nDepiction rules:\\n- God the Father has no human face or body; use light, cloud, fire or radiance. The Holy Spirit is dove, wind or flame, never human.\\n- Treat battles, death and crucifixion seriously; avoid lingering gore.\\n- No sexually explicit content; non-sexual nudity may follow the text.\\n- Show all peoples with dignity, without ethnic or religious caricature.\\n- Visionary creatures follow the text, strange and fearsome rather than comic.\\nEra: Egypt, wilderness and settlement. People: Israelites, Egyptians and neighboring ancient peoples. Dress: Woven tunics, cloaks, Egyptian linen and priestly garments. Buildings and objects: Tents, tabernacle, Egyptian palaces and fortified towns.\\n\\nSTORY SECTION: The golden calf\\nON STAGE: Aaron, Moses\\nTEXT OF THE SECTION'S FIRST MOMENT (the look covers the whole section):\\nHe received what they handed him, fashioned it with an engraving tool, and made it a molded calf.\"}],\"response_format\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"section_look\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\